    "q-70485": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70485",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x-2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242844/assets/e3f5ed500c81d09e2775f09fd10a221d7ec0fca7e39249b7add7a680328b68c1.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x-2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ to the *right* by $2$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated to the right by $2$ units, the vertical asymptote $x=0$ is also translated to the right by $2$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242844/assets/c575c9898d27a6bf612d89655fcb78328a25333088588de9a4c8fe54944c26aa.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
