    "q-16362": {
      "dom_id": "step-q16362",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x+4}+2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $+4$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $4$ units to the *left*, and\n\n- the $+2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242844/assets/851b90f3d442a528ccc2441f0c15e3ef344be9ee54c6789b312673a5ee7ae06f.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
